Report this machine's connection, token storage and expiry, default target, backend and installed CLI version.
By default, one public request with a three-second timeout reports backend status and compares the installed and advertised CLI versions. The completion time is saved for that backend even if the check fails.
Use --offline to show local readiness and the last check time without sending requests or writing state. Neither mode accesses the keychain, reads or unlocks a stored token, prompts or detects server-side revocation.
Passphrase storage is reported as locked unless THE_AGENT_CLI_TOKEN is set, even when THE_AGENT_CLI_PASSPHRASE is available. Expired tokens require reconnecting.

Example offline report (macOS, before the first online check):
✓ Connected as Example User (workstation)
  Device ID         6b8f0d3e-2a1c-4e55-9a37-0c1d2e3f4a5b
  Token storage     macOS Keychain
  Token expiry      2027-02-14 10:21 (in 3 months)
  Default chat      3f2a9c1e7b6d4a58b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7 (telegram · Example Chat, private)
  Backend           localhost
  Local CLI         1.2.3
  Last checked      never checked

Use agent-cli connect <KEY> to connect this machine.

Usage: agent-cli status

Flags:
      --offline  Show local readiness and last check time without sending requests
  -h, --help     Print help
  -v, --verbose  Print diagnostic details to stderr

Examples:
  agent-cli status
  agent-cli status --offline

Environment: THE_AGENT_CLI_HOME, THE_AGENT_CLI_API_URL, THE_AGENT_CLI_TOKEN, THE_AGENT_CLI_DEFAULT_CHAT, THE_AGENT_CLI_DEFAULT_PLATFORM
Exit codes: 0 locally connected · 1 local state unusable or operational failure · 2 usage or default validation error · 3 not connected, locked, expired or invalid environment token. Backend health does not affect the exit code.
